WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.680
<i>I haven't been able to sleep since our arrival.</i>

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.180
<i>As Silver's cannon hung above our fort,</i>

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.530
<i>he demanded of us to give him the treasure map.</i>

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.940
<i>In reality, the cannon was nothing but an ordinary piece of wood.</i>

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.470
<i>Of course, it was I who discovered the trick!</i>

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.580
<i>However, seeing as his trick failed,
Silver proceeded with his plan's next phase.</i>

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.810
<i>And unfortunately, his new strategy cost us very dear.</i>

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.560
<i>After old Redruth, Joyce was the next one to leave us.</i>

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:55.560
<i>Even our leader, Captain Smollett, took a bullet to the shoulder.</i>

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.500
Captain Silver, shouldn't you rest a bit?
Daybreak is almost upon us.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.020
What's happening at the fort?
Any developments?

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.170
N-No, sir...

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:18.380
Nothing new happening.
Nothing's changed.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:22.020
You followed my instructions during the attack on the fort?

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.320
Y-Yes, we've done as you said.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:29.270
I see. So they still haven't noticed anything yet.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.900
This isn't good...
He has a high fever.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.020
Okay, we must extract
the bullet immediately.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:40.830
Jim.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:41.280
Yes?

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.250
Hurry and boil some water.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.500
Yes, sir!

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:10.350
It's horrible! They threw
dead animals in the well!

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.390
We're done for! We can no longer use the well water!

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.030
Treasure
Island

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:35.830
Takarajima

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.640
saa ikou

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.640
Come, let's go

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.730
yume ni mita shima heto

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.730
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.570
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.570
Across the waves, on the wind

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:54.450
umi hedeyou

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:54.450
We'll travel the oceans

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.370
ikute ni wa

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.370
Many of us

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.370
minna mada shiranai

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.370
Still don't know of

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.120
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.120
The days and nights full of mystery

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.620
matte iru darou

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.620
That await us there

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.130
itsumo shinji you

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.130
We must always have trust

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.380
magokoro wo

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.380
And be sincere

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:19.640
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:19.640
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.770
tade hitotsu no

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.770
I only...

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.190
akogare dake wa

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.190
...have one desire

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.480
doko no dare ni mo

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.480
And no one...

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:35.190
kese wa shinai sa

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:35.190
...will ever take it away

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:41.740
tade hitotsu no

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:41.740
I only...

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.040
akogare dake wa

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.040
...have one desire

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.370
doko no dare ni mo

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.370
And no one...

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:54.300
kese wa shinai sa

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:54.300
...will ever take it away

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.540
episode

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.540
Surrender, Silver-Style

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.580
Listen.
They don't have water anymore.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.840
So if they want any, they'll have to leave.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.980
We'll pierce them like strainers when that happens!

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.460
His condition is worsening.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.820
Without boiled water,

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:26.020
it'll be impossible to disinfect
the wound and the instruments.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.490
What will happen if we don't do anything?

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:32.620
If I can't extract the bullet from him...

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.100
...the infection might spread
throughout his entire body.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.780
Like Redruth and Joyce, we'll lose another man.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.310
It's only a matter of time.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.200
Dr. Livesey.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.170
We have to get water somehow, don't we?

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.850
It's the only way!

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:52.810
Jim...

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.770
The well may be useless,
but there's still the river!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.360
Yes, but to go there we'll have to leave the fort, and then—

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.090
We'll deal with that then!

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:05.150
Silver's men are outside, ready to ambush us.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.740
I know that!
But I have to go anyway!

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.050
<i>I have a good idea!</i>

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.800
<i>If I climb the wall,
I'll be the perfect target.</i>

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:22.210
<i>But if I go underneath they won't expect anything.</i>

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:25.470
That's it, Jim!
That's a brilliant idea!

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:28.090
Alrighty, give me that!
I'm going to dig a hole.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.860
How about now?
Have they moved?

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:42.820
No, not as of yet.
It's all dead quiet.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:48.570
<i>"Dead quiet..."
I see.</i>

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:53.200
Okay then, half of us will stay here to stake-out the fort.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.500
What?
Half of us?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:54.910
Yes.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.710
The other half will follow me.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.120
T-To go where?

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:02.170
To the river of course.
Isn't that obvious, idiot!

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.750
Okay, give it to me!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.760
We're counting on you, Jim.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:14.640
Had I been a little thinner,
I would have accompanied you.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.180
Peace!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.600
Yes, that's it, peace...

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.620
I can't take any more...

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:32.580
You clever little...!

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.950
Good, we made it!
Now it'll be just fine.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:17.560
We're going to save Captain Smollett.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:18.670
Come on...

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.300
Hey, Jim!

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.050
Silver!

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.960
How's Captain Smollett?

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.010
He's hurt badly, isn't he?

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:43.570
Without water, that quack
Dr. Livesey can't operate, right?

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:50.320
Honestly, risking your life in order to save Smollett is stupid!

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:55.280
You know you'll die of thirst sooner or later.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.420
D-Damn you...!

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.100
What are you waiting for?

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:08.340
Hurry and raise the jug or you won't have any water left.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.200
Silver!

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.880
Don't look at me like that, Jim.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.520
This is war.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:46.170
The meanest and strongest always prove victorious.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:47.630
You're wrong!

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.090
It's not the meanest or strongest who win!

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.590
It's the good guys!

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.600
The good guys?

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.340
Jim!
You've got it backwards.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:02.720
Good and evil aren't predefined roles!

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.910
In our world, it's those who survive that become good!

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:16.500
Damn you!

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.920
Jim, return to the fort and tell them this:

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:23.540
"If you want water, then give us the map."

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.660
Give them the map.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:53.980
Captain Smollett's life is at stake.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.470
I'm going to parley with Silver!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.050
What are you doing, Gray?!

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.220
Isn't it possible to operate without water?

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:25.640
I didn't want to say this in front of Dr. Livesey,

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.530
but it's something that I've seen being done during the war.

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:32.610
I'm talking about operations where they extract bullets without using water.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.140
I want to know, Gray.
Please tell me.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:38.000
No, it's not like I know everything.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.540
I'm always eager to learn,
to further improve myself.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.490
Instead of water, we use fire.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.660
Instead of a knife, we use a hot iron rod.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:51.130
That way, we can open the flesh and extract the bullet.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.320
There will be great scarring,

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:58.050
but once the wound is cauterized, the patient's life will be spared.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.010
Alright, let's give it a try!

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:10.190
What is it, Gray?
You're early for your shift.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:15.450
Th-That's not it... I just don't
like the smell of grilled meat.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:19.800
There's a barbecue for dinner?
Are you serious?

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.660
No, that's not what I meant.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.750
Got it?
Hold him down firmly.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:28.320
Understood!

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:29.160
Count on us.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.950
We did it!
It was successful!

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:07.490
Benbow, you shouldn't!
The well water isn't drinkable!

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:12.830
Hold on! You're not the only one who's thirsty.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:27.810
What is it, Jim? Has something happened to Captain Smollett?

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:32.530
No, the captain's sound asleep. I've come to take my shift.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.440
I see.
That's kind of you.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:37.330
No, it's nothing...

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:41.150
This is war.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.830
We're overwhelmed by fatigue, thirst and lack of sleep,

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.950
but we can't complain.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:55.330
Oh, well.

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:15.820
Mother!
And Lily, too!

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:19.050
Jim, when did you return from Treasure Island?

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:20.860
Yes, you could have told your poor mother.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:24.820
You're right, I'm sorry.
I was just a little thirsty.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:28.450
You're so mean! You didn't even send any letters!

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.120
That's right, my bad.
I didn't since I was so thirsty.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:35.530
Don't tell me... Did you forget about your poor mother?

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:40.660
No, I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.
I was just... so thirsty.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:42.900
Let me quench my thirst first.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:46.300
Then I'll tell you everything.
Yes, that's what we'll do!

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.020
I've found it!

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.270
Time to drink!

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.280
Silver!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:15.910
Wait, Silver!

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:26.670
Water, Mother...

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:30.540
Water...
Lily! Mother!

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.460
Lilly!

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:34.350
Mother!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.210
It's all over!
I'm going to die of thirst...

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.200
Rain clouds!

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:07.470
Darn, it can't be.
They're one lucky bunch.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.590
It's raining!

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:25.070
It's raining!

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.070
It's raining!

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:32.960
Now we don't have to worry about water!

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:35.990
Yes, this time we must
thank the heavens, Jim.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.130
Rain falls on Treasure Island.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.760
It soaks the warriors and closes their hearts.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:55.480
O rain, are you a good omen or sign of misfortune?

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.340
That's enough, Abraham!

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.600
Believe in the word of God.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:03.310
Do not doubt the miracles that he's capable of.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:09.780
Flint, my idea of luring them out by thirst is a total failure.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:14.910
With this rainfall, they'll have enough to drink for a whole week.

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:19.000
Don't mock me, Flint.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.760
I'm thinking of a new plan.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:23.210
C-Captain Silver!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:24.520
What is it, Morgan?

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:28.840
Th-The thing is... Big Eyes and
The Barrel are acting strange. Yes!

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:42.560
Look, they haven't moved for a long time.

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.980
Idiot, of course they haven't.
They're dead!

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:50.440
<i>The malaria has taken two victims.</i>

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.920
Tell me, is anyone else suffering a fever?

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:57.360
Yes, the bosun, Anderson, has been for a while...

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:00.620
And Monkey Face has caught it, we think.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:04.480
Oh, the men are soaked
and their bodies feverish.

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:08.200
We poor devils, will die
under the Southern Cross.

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:10.720
Believe in the word of God!

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:13.550
And sing His miracles!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.840
Hey, don't you think Abraham is acting weird?

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.440
He could have caught malaria, too.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:18.930
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.780
Captain Smollett.

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:36.120
Livesey, my friend.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:39.740
I've caused you all a lot of trouble, it seems.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.330
What are you saying?
None of us think that.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.710
No, this isn't befitting of a leader.
I'm truly sorry.

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:49.370
But don't you worry any longer.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:53.240
Captain, you're not ready to get up.

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:57.320
I must make up for time lost and work twice as hard.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.400
Come now, captain.

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:02.810
Where are Mr. Trelawney and Hunter?
Did the enemy get them too?

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.000
Don't say that, captain.
They're outside.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.760
They're on guard.

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:09.190
Really?
How stupid of me.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:14.650
Caught a cold?

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.830
No, I don't think so...

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.960
<i>It's our first night of rain on the island.</i>

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:23.160
<i>It's also our first peaceful night.</i>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.600
<i>There's no longer need for worry about Captain Smollett...</i>

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:30.770
<i>...and I realize it's been a long time
since I've been able to sleep soundly.</i>

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:48.190
On your feet, mates!
I have a new plan!

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:49.650
A-Aye, sir!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.480
Wh-What time is it?

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:53.950
Wh-What is it?

00:18:56.240 --> 00:19:00.080
Puppy, go look for the men who are staking out the fort. Hurry!

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.820
A-Aye-aye, sir!

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.800
You want to move the Hispaniola?

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:18.550
That's right. The cannons aren't
accurate enough from this distance.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:21.510
That's why we're going to move it closer.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.930
W-Wait a minute.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:27.560
If we go any closer, we'll hit the reef.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.850
Don't tell me you forgot?

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:32.040
I haven't forgotten.
You're absolutely right.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:35.360
We'd definitely hit the reefs by
moving the ship the normal way.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:37.530
However, I have a plan.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.820
That's why I woke you all up.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:41.820
We'll pull it.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.780
We're going to take the rowboats and pull it very gently.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:48.790
By moving slowly, we'll be able to avoid the reefs.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:52.250
What do you think of my idea, eh, mates?

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:56.290
Wait, pulling a boat is slave work!

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:58.640
We're all exhausted as is.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:01.170
We don't want to end up like Big Eyes and The Barrel!

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:14.010
So George, you don't want Flint's treasure anymore?

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:15.760
N-No, of course I do.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:19.440
Really? Then I don't want to hear you whining.

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:21.600
Our dear treasure...

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:25.320
I'm trying to find a way for us to share it.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.400
Try to understand me.

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.830
Y-Yes...
I-I understand completely, leader.

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:34.790
Very well, anyone else need an explanation?

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.950
Good, that's the way!
Keep going like that!

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:11.430
My old friend, Flint. I'll show you how to destroy a fort.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:17.360
Fire!

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:32.620
To      be        continued

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:37.410
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:37.410
Hey sea breeze

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:43.220
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:43.220
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:49.430
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:49.430
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:54.870
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:54.870
A word to my dear mother

00:22:54.870 --> 00:23:00.280
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:54.870 --> 00:23:00.280
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:05.740
kaban ippai no

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:05.740
And that my bag filled

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:11.370
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:11.370
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:17.230
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:17.230
Will be brought back

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:23.820
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:23.820
The sunset on my back

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:29.710
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:29.710
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:39.430
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:39.430
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:47.280
The enemy's cannon echoes.

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:50.980
I must cut the ship's moorings
if I want to save the fort.

00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:54.820
On Ben Gunn's rowboat
I head for the Hispaniola.

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:58.560
As it turns out, this worthless thing has a will of its own.

00:23:58.560 --> 00:24:01.560
On top of that, sharks are approaching!

00:24:01.560 --> 00:24:03.800
Oh no, I'm in big trouble!

00:24:03.800 --> 00:24:06.600
Next time on Treasure Island:
"We're Castaways...!?"

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:08.920
Don't lose track of the story!

